# Native production settings panel with a fake pairing backend: no credentials, tailnet or real work.
fold folded
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --ez phoneRunner true
clearlog
expect Let a computer reach this phone
expect jacks-mac-pro
expect macbook-pro
expect Phone D stays mail only
nolog fixture pairing tap
shot phone-runner-pairing-cover
tap [ pair ]
expect Pairing file sent
log fixture pairing tap
expect unpair
shot phone-runner-paired-cover
tap [ unpair ]
expect Its key no longer works
log fixture unpair tap
fold unfolded
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview
shell am start -n dev.omalauncher.artifactpreview/.PreviewActivity --ez phoneRunner true
expect Let a computer reach this phone
expect jacks-mac-pro
shot phone-runner-pairing-unfolded
rotate landscape
expect macbook-pro
expect Close phone sessions
shot phone-runner-pairing-sideways
[phone] After promotion and approved helper deployment: Settings > phone sessions. No pairing happens before the owner's Pair tap. Pair one owned Mac; Taildrop file goes only to that Mac, imports into desktop RunnerKeys, key is never shown/logged/mailed; Fold stores only a device-bound digest. In desktop select Fold: builder-a/b/c, phone-d and local phone chats appear; no duplicate Mac chats or Soma front agent. Server binds only the concrete Tailscale IP on8478: no LAN/wildcard listener.
[phone] From paired desktop, send one harmless builder prompt; verify now/queued position and exact words in the correct tab. Read cursor events, reconnect real SSE stream without growing retry delays, stop task + queued work and verify desktop reports stop successful (stopped:true); Phone D is readable/stoppable but sending is403. No other session stops. Keyless, wrong key, correct key from wrong device and non-owner whois must401 on health/list/read/write. Unpair immediately refuses key and closes its stream. No live prompts without Boss's explicit test OK.
[phone] With one harmless native question/approval: only owner's desktop tap POSTs. Wrong nonce403 and malformed form400 leave card waiting. Valid answer or question Skip must be reported successful by desktop (decision field parsed), resumes once via existing approval reply, clears phone card/notification/NeedsYou; replay404. Verify all questions get delegation text on Skip, not stop/blank denial. Race two devices and lock phone: no duplicate answer or bypass. Sleep/off-tailnet reports Fold unreachable; helper outages follow the bounded identity rule below.

[phone] After owner-approved pairing: with the helper offline, the same desktop key and confirmed address work within seven days without extending the confirmation timestamp; changed address, expired proof and an explicit helper refusal fail closed. Loopback and the phone Linux connecting to its own tailnet IP must401 even with a fixture valid credential and nonce; no approval is forwarded. Restore helper and confirm a fresh owner/device proof renews the lease. Use test fixtures for expiry; never expose production keys.
